-chain-depth must be at least 1: a smaller value is a usage error.
-- args --
-chain-depth=0 a.go:1:1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
errtrace: invalid -chain-depth 0 (want at least 1)
usage: errtrace [flags] <target>

errtrace reports the Error Set of a Target: every Error Origin that can reach
the Target's error result, with its Propagation Path.

<target> is a position in a Go file, with byte columns:
  file.go:LINE:COL | file.go:#OFFSET | file.go:L:C-L2:C2 (the start is used)

flags:
  -chain-depth N
    	max Wrap Chain depth N before truncation (default 8)
  -p patterns
    	comma-separated package patterns to load (default "./...")
  -tags list
    	comma-separated list of build tags
-- exit --
2
-- go.mod --
module example.com/fx

go 1.24
-- a.go --
package fx
